text:
Where automation happens

html`&lt;div class="tiles"&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value" style="color:#b4463c"&gt;${summary.radar_runs_successful}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;successful unattended runs of the two radars, ${d3.utcFormat("%-d %b")(new Date(summary.radar_runs_first))} to ${d3.utcFormat("%-d %b %Y")(new Date(summary.radar_runs_as_of))} (${summary.radar_runs_scheduled} scheduled) &lt;span class="status measured"&gt;measured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`






The research radar and the team’s news radar run every day on a schedule, with no one involved. Each reads its sources, verifies and archives what it finds, and writes a report. No one did that work by hand before, so it is automation and task creation at once: new tasks performed by machines. Runs that fail stop without publishing anything, by design.

In numbers

summary = FileAttachment("data/summary.json").json()
fmt = d3.format(",")
day = s =&gt; d3.utcFormat("%-d %b")(new Date(s))
tip = (text, definition) =&gt; `&lt;span class="term" tabindex="0" data-tip="${definition}"&gt;${text}&lt;/span&gt;`
html`&lt;div class="tiles"&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${summary.valued_entries}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;${tip("tasks", "One task is one finished piece of work done with the agent, logged with my hours, an estimate of the hours without AI, a quality score and the outcome.")} with my hours and assessment&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.valued_first)} to ${day(summary.valued_last)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${fmt(summary.hours_actual_logged)} h&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;my time on those tasks&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.valued_first)} to ${day(summary.valued_last)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile gold"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${summary.hours_saved_lower_bound}–${summary.hours_saved_raw} h&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;${tip("saved", "On tasks that would have been done anyway: my estimate of the hours without AI, minus the hours with it. The lower figure counts only estimates I was highly confident in and wrote down within a week of the work.")} on ${summary.substitution_with_numbers} tasks that would have been done anyway&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.valued_first)} to ${day(summary.valued_last)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile teal"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${fmt(summary.expansion_hours)} h&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;on ${summary.expansion_tasks} ${tip("tasks that would not exist without AI", "Expansion: work I would not have done at all without an agent. It has no time-saved figure, because there is nothing to compare it with.")}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.valued_first)} to ${day(summary.valued_last)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile green"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${fmt(summary.usage_tool_calls)}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;${tip("agent actions", "An agent action (tool call) is one thing the agent did on its own: reading a file, running code, searching the web, editing a document. Counted from the agent's session logs.")} &lt;span class="status measured"&gt;measured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.usage_first_day)} to ${day(summary.usage_last_day)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile green"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${summary.radar_runs_successful}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="label"&gt;${tip("unattended runs", "Daily runs of the two radars on a schedule, with no one involved: each reads its sources, checks and archives what it finds, and writes a report. Counted from GitHub.")} of the two radars &lt;span class="status measured"&gt;measured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="period"&gt;${day(summary.radar_runs_first)} to ${day(summary.radar_runs_as_of)}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`




































Why the periods differ. I have used the agent since June. The agent deletes its session records after 30 days unless a session is reopened. I first saved them on 8 September, so usage before about 9 August survives only for sessions I reopened later; the oldest is from 22 July. June and most of July are not recorded. Since 8 September everything is kept. My hours and assessments come from the weekly log, which started on 25 September; the first tasks in it date from 10 September. Work from June to early September appears on this site only as measured usage, not as valued tasks.
Hours, time saved and quality are my own estimates; usage and radar runs are measured. Each figure is labelled on the results pages.

Time saved on work that would have happened anyway
For each substitution task: my hours with AI (dot) and my estimate of the hours without it (ring). The gap is the time saved. self-reported estimates

subs = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.value_type === "substitution" && d.hours_counterfactual !== null)
  .map(d =&gt; ({...d, label: `${d.date.slice(5)} · ${truncate(d.title.replace(/^Project /, ""), 46)}`, lower: d.confidence === "high" && d.logged !== "backfilled"}))
saved = ({raw: d3.sum(subs, d =&gt; d.hours_counterfactual - d.hours_actual), lower: d3.sum(subs.filter(d =&gt; d.lower), d =&gt; d.hours_counterfactual - d.hours_actual)})
html`&lt;div class="tiles"&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile gold"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.format(".1f")(d3.sum(subs, d =&gt; d.hours_counterfactual) / d3.sum(subs, d =&gt; d.hours_actual))}×&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;hours the work would have taken without AI, for each hour it took with AI&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile gold"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${saved.raw} h&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;saved on ${subs.length} tasks&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile gold"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${saved.lower} h&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;cautious figure: only the ${subs.filter(d =&gt; d.lower).length} tasks where I was highly confident in my estimate and wrote it down within a week of the work&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`























Plot.plot({
  marginLeft: 330, height: Math.max(200, 22 * subs.length + 40), width: 720, style: {fontSize: "11px"},
  x: {label: "Hours", grid: true},
  y: {label: null, domain: subs.map(d =&gt; d.label)},
  marks: [
    Plot.link(subs, {x1: "hours_actual", x2: "hours_counterfactual", y: "label", stroke: "#9fb3c8"}),
    Plot.dot(subs, {x: "hours_counterfactual", y: "label", r: 5, stroke: "#005da8", fill: d =&gt; d.lower ? "#005da8" : "white", tip: true,
      title: d =&gt; `${d.title}\nwith AI: ${d.hours_actual} h\nwithout AI (estimate): ${d.hours_counterfactual} h\nconfidence: ${d.confidence}, logged ${d.logged === "at_time" ? "within a week" : "later"}`}),
    Plot.dot(subs, {x: "hours_actual", y: "label", r: 4, fill: "#17202a"})
  ]
})







Filled rings are the tasks in the cautious figure.

Work that would not exist without AI
Expansion tasks have no time-saved figure: there is no version of the work done without AI to compare with. These are simply the hours I put into work that would not have happened otherwise. self-reported

exp = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.value_type === "expansion")
expQ = exp.filter(d =&gt; d.quality !== null)
html`&lt;div class="tiles"&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile teal"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.sum(exp, d =&gt; d.hours_actual)} h&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;of my time on ${exp.length} expansion tasks&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile teal"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.format(".0%")(d3.sum(exp, d =&gt; d.hours_actual) / d3.sum(rows, d =&gt; d.hours_actual))}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;of all my logged hours&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile teal"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.format(".1f")(d3.mean(expQ, d =&gt; d.quality))}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;mean quality of these tasks (3 = my own unaided standard)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`























Plot.plot({
  height: 260, width: 720,
  x: {label: null, type: "band", tickFormat: monthName},
  y: {label: "Hours", grid: true},
  color: {domain: ["substitution", "expansion"], range: ["#005da8", "#008c95"], legend: true, tickFormat: d =&gt; valueLabel[d]},
  marks: [
    Plot.barY(rows.filter(d =&gt; d.value_type === "substitution" || d.value_type === "expansion"),
      Plot.groupX({y: "sum"}, {x: "month", y: "hours_actual", fill: "value_type", tip: true})),
    Plot.ruleY([0])
  ]
})

Quality and rework
Quality is scored against my own unaided standard: 1 is clearly worse, 3 the same, 5 clearly better. Rework is the part of my time spent fixing the agent’s output. self-reported

q = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.quality !== null)
rw = rows.filter(d =&gt; d.rework_hours !== null)
html`&lt;div class="tiles"&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.format(".1f")(d3.mean(q, d =&gt; d.quality))}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;mean quality, ${q.length} tasks&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${d3.format(".0%")(d3.sum(rw, d =&gt; d.rework_hours) / d3.sum(rw, d =&gt; d.hours_actual))}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;of my time was rework (${d3.sum(rw, d =&gt; d.rework_hours)} of ${d3.sum(rw, d =&gt; d.hours_actual)} h)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;div class="value"&gt;${rw.filter(d =&gt; d.rework_hours &gt; 0).length} of ${rw.length}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="label"&gt;tasks needed some rework&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`























Plot.plot({
  height: 220, width: 720,
  x: {label: "Quality score (3 = my own unaided standard)", domain: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], type: "band"},
  y: {label: "Tasks", grid: true},
  marks: [
    Plot.barY(q, Plot.groupX({y: "count"}, {x: "quality", fill: "#005da8", tip: true})),
    Plot.ruleY([0])
  ]
})
